---
/* Component — DisplayCardTitle
 * The card's heading. Keeps daisyUI's own .card-title class — rented
 * deliberately for its flex row (display:flex; align-items:center; gap:.5rem)
 * — and re-skins only the typography. bravoixr's rule is unlayered and so beats
 * daisyUI's @layer daisyui one, the same mechanism PageHeader relies on for
 * .navbar.
 *
 * Content comes through a slot rather than a title prop: the rented flex row
 * exists precisely so a title can sit beside an icon or a trailing element,
 * which a string prop would forbid. This differs from PageSection, where the
 * title is a prop — there the heading is plain text by design.
 *
 * Heading level is hardcoded to <h3>, matching today's markup and the
 * hardcode-no-level-prop precedent set by PageSection (<h2>) and PageSubSection
 * (<h3>). Known limitation: a card inside a PageSubSection repeats <h3> at the
 * same level as its container. Left as-is rather than adding the system's first
 * level prop; revisit if the outline becomes a real problem. */
---

<h3 class="card-title">
  <slot />
</h3>

<style>
  .card-title {
    font-family: var(--bravoixr-font-heading);
    font-size: var(--bravoixr-text-context-title);
    font-weight: var(--bravoixr-weight-subsection-title);
    line-height: var(--bravoixr-leading-display);
    letter-spacing: var(--bravoixr-tracking-display);
    margin-block: 0 var(--bravoixr-spacing-3);
  }
</style>
